# Build-context exclusions for the repo-root context.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS IN ADDITION TO deploy/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `deploy/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` is the BuildKit/Buildx convention:
# the builder looks for `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` next to the -f path.
# The CLASSIC builder (what you get from `docker build` when the buildx
# component is not installed) ignores that file entirely and reads only a
# repo-root `.dockerignore`.
#
# Consequence when this file is absent: a local `pnpm install` leaves
# `web/node_modules/` on the host, the classic builder ships it in the
# context, and the Dockerfile's `COPY web/ ./web/` overlays it on top of the
# Linux `node_modules` that `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter web`
# just created. The web stage then dies with:
#
#   Error: Cannot find module '/web/web/node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js'
#   [ERR_PNPM_RECURSIVE_RUN_FIRST_FAIL] web@0.0.0 build: `vite build`
#
# Keep this list in sync with deploy/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
# Everything the Dockerfile COPYs must stay included; see the notes below.

# ── Node dependency trees ────────────────────────────────
# The single most important entry. Also covers the nested workspace
# installs (web/electron, editors/vscode, sdks/web-extension,
# deploy/cloudflare, .github/ci-deps) via the unanchored pattern.
**/node_modules/

# ── VCS + IDE ────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# ── Python build outputs ─────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/

# ── Test + dev artifacts ─────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log

# ── Local databases / large blobs ────────────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite
mlflow.db
conv_*

# ── Electron desktop lane ────────────────────────────────
# The web-builder stage COPYs ONLY web/electron/package.json (so the pnpm
# workspace is structurally complete). The rest of that tree is ~470 MB of
# desktop build output and is never referenced by the image. Excluding it
# keeps the context small without affecting the server build.
web/electron/dist/
web/electron/out/
web/electron/release/

web/electron/.vite/

# ── Repo directories the image never reads ───────────────
# NOTE: web/, omnigent/, sdks/, examples/, deploy/ and the root manifests
# ARE copied by the Dockerfile — do not add those here.
tests/
loadtest/
demos/
scripts/
dev/
designs/
skills/
docs/
.claude/

# ── Docs and metadata not needed at runtime ──────────────
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
openapi.json

# ── Deploy trees that are not part of the container image ─
# deploy/docker/ IS needed (entrypoint.py, install-harness-cli.sh).
deploy/databricks/
deploy/aws/
